From 1615b2c77f379045b1247de2a8e400f9926447ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mingyang Sun (Public)" <Mingyang.Sun@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:45:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] HIP: enable OCP FP4/FP6 hardware builtins for gfx1250-strict

Same defect as the FP8 guards, in the MX/OCP headers. Both
amd_hip_mx_common.h and amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp derive
HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS and HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS from
__gfx1250__ alone, so a gfx1250-strict build gets:

  HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS = 0
  HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS = 1   (host conversion path on device)

That macro gates the hardware builtin at ~103 sites:

  amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp   67
  amd_hip_fp6.h        20
  amd_hip_fp4.h        16

so FP4 and FP6 conversions silently lose their hardware paths on strict,
in the same way FP8 did.

Recognise the strict variant in both guards, in both headers. The two
headers define the same macros, so they must stay consistent; both are
updated together. Only a macro exclusive to gfx1250-strict is added, so
no other target changes behaviour.

Measured on MI455X (gfx1250), ROCm 10.1.0 / HIP 7.16.26362, counting
hardware conversion instructions in the generated device ISA for a
standalone __hip_fp4_e2m1 / __hip_fp6_e2m3 kernel:

                            v_cvt_*fp4*   v_cvt_*fp6*
  gfx1250                        1             1
  gfx1250-strict, before         0             0
  gfx1250-strict, after          1             1   (parity with gfx1250)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h     | 4 ++--
 projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
index e2d74d87f61..82eba78fa12 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_mx_common.h
@@ -10,12 +10,12 @@
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX950_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if defined(__gfx1250__)
+#if defined(__gfx1250__) || defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if !defined(__gfx950__) && !defined(__gfx1250__)
+#if !defined(__gfx950__) && !defined(__gfx1250__) && !defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 0
diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
index 5b199c27893..54fe59bfa44 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_ocp_fp.hpp
@@ -30,12 +30,12 @@ static_assert(sizeof(__hip_uint64_t) * CHAR_BIT == 64);
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX950_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if defined(__gfx1250__)
+#if defined(__gfx1250__) || defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_GFX1250_OCP_BUILTINS 0
 #endif
-#if !defined(__gfx950__) and !defined(__gfx1250__)
+#if !defined(__gfx950__) and !defined(__gfx1250__) and !defined(__gfx1250_strict__)
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 1
 #else
 #define HIP_ENABLE_HOST_OCP_CONVERSIONS 0
